course: dictionary
lesson: 6134
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Mike is a boy's name, but it is also an informal word for a microphone, and it is the code word for the letter M. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Mike's mum has three children: April, May and...» This sentence is about people in a family, so Mike is a name, short for Michael. «At Christmas dinner Uncle Mike says "Bulls hate red!"» is also a name, because Uncle Mike is a person.
explain: Now picture a school assembly. If someone says «Speak into the mike, the mike is on», a mike is a microphone that picks up your voice so it can be made louder or recorded. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence and see if it makes sense.
fact: Mike is a first name, short for Michael.
fact: (informal) A mike is a microphone, the device that picks up your voice.
fact: (informal) To mike someone up means to fix a small microphone on them.
fact: In the radio alphabet, Mike stands for the letter M, and pilots and police say it when spelling over the radio.
fact: The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning to choose.
exercise: «Mike's mum has three children: April, May and...» Who is Mike in this sentence? | A small car | A microphone that makes voices louder | The letter M in the radio alphabet | *A boy's name, short for Michael
exercise: «The mike is on, so speak clearly.» What is a mike in this sentence? | The letter M | Uncle Mike | A bicycle bell | *A microphone
exercise: Pilots say "Mike" when they spell words over the radio. What does Mike stand for? | The letter N | A boy's first name only | A microphone | *The letter M
test: «Please mike the speaker before the play starts.» What does mike mean here? | Paint the stage | *Put a microphone on | Give a big hug | Lose the voice
test: Which meaning of Mike fits «Uncle Mike says "Bulls hate red!" for the tenth year running»? | The letter M | A microphone | A radio code word | *A person's name
exam: «Tonight is open mike night, so bring a song to sing.» In this sentence, what is a mike? | A letter of the alphabet | *A microphone | A boy's name | A bicycle
